IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `roc-core`
IMPORT `roc-definitions`

-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 11: production of documents.  Part roc2, layer 1.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT: see roc2-order-9a.l4 and NOTES.md ("Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (roc2)").
-- Every answer is subject to O 3 r 2(1) (roc1): the Court's discretion to order otherwise.
-- The count of a period is O 3 r 3 (roc1): every period function takes `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`.
-- Order-local terms (r 2(2) "known adverse documents", r 3(1) "requested documents") are declared here.
-- The Ideals (r 1(2)) are the keel's `o 1 r 3(1) an objective is one of the Ideals`.

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 11, Rule 1 -- scope of Order and the Court's power`
-- ===========================================================================

DECLARE `o 11 r 1(1) a thing this Order might affect` IS ONE OF
    `o 11 r 1(1)(a) an agreement that the parties or any set of parties may make to broaden the scope of such obligations`
    `o 11 r 1(1)(b) the Court's power to allow a broader scope of discovery where it is in the interests of justice to do so`
    `o 11 r 1(1) any other thing`

-- src:1114 | 1. —(1) This Order sets out the basic requirements of the parties’ obligations to produce and exchange documents and does not affect — ( a )
-- src:1115 | any agreement that the parties or any set of parties may make to broaden the scope of such obligations; or
-- src:1116 | ( b )
-- src:1117 | the Court’s power to allow a broader scope of discovery where it is in the interests of justice to do so.
@ref O 11 r 1(1) (src:1114-1117)
GIVEN thing IS A `o 11 r 1(1) a thing this Order might affect`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 11 r 1(1) this Order affects this` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `o 11 r 1(1)(a) an agreement that the parties or any set of parties may make to broaden the scope of such obligations` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Order ... does not affect" (a) any agreement ... to broaden the scope (flat negative, ruling N2)
    WHEN `o 11 r 1(1)(b) the Court's power to allow a broader scope of discovery where it is in the interests of justice to do so` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Order ... does not affect" (b) the Court's power to allow a broader scope (flat negative, ruling N2)
    WHEN `o 11 r 1(1) any other thing` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph names (a) and (b); it does not say what else this Order affects

DECLARE `o 11 r 1(2) a principle the Court must bear in mind` IS ONE OF
    `o 11 r 1(2) the Ideals`
    `o 11 r 1(2)(a) that a claimant is to sue and proceed on the strength of the claimant's case and not on the weakness of the defendant's case`
    `o 11 r 1(2)(b) that a party who sues or is sued in court does not thereby give up the party's right to privacy and confidentiality in the party's documents and communications`

-- src:1118 | (2) In exercising its power in this Order, the Court must bear in mind, in addition to the Ideals, the following principles: ( a )
-- src:1119 | that a claimant is to sue and proceed on the strength of the claimant’s case and not on the weakness of the defendant’s case;
-- src:1120 | ( b )
-- src:1121 | that a party who sues or is sued in court does not thereby give up the party’s right to privacy and confidentiality in the party’s documents and communications.
@ref O 11 r 1(2) (src:1118-1121)
GIVEN `the Court is exercising its power in this Order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is an application for a broader scope of discovery` IS A BOOLEAN
      principle IS A `o 11 r 1(2) a principle the Court must bear in mind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 11 r 1(2) the Court must bear this principle in mind` MEANS
    IF `the Court is exercising its power in this Order`
    THEN
        CONSIDER principle
        WHEN `o 11 r 1(2) the Ideals` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 11 r 1(2)(a) that a claimant is to sue and proceed on the strength of the claimant's case and not on the weakness of the defendant's case` THEN
            IF `there is an application for a broader scope of discovery`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): paragraph (5) "paragraph (2) does not apply" on an application for a broader scope of discovery (flat negative, ruling N2)
            ELSE JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 11 r 1(2)(b) that a party who sues or is sued in court does not thereby give up the party's right to privacy and confidentiality in the party's documents and communications` THEN
            IF `there is an application for a broader scope of discovery`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): paragraph (5) "paragraph (2) does not apply" on an application for a broader scope of discovery (flat negative, ruling N2)
            ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In exercising its power in this Order"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

-- src:1122 | (3) The Court may allow a broader scope of discovery where the Court determines that it is in the interests of justice to do so.
@ref O 11 r 1(3) (src:1122)
GIVEN `the Court determines that it is in the interests of justice to allow a broader scope of discovery` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 11 r 1(3) the Court may allow a broader scope of discovery` MEANS
    IF `the Court determines that it is in the interests of justice to allow a broader scope of discovery`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the Court determines that it is in the interests of justice to do so" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))

-- src:1123 | (4) It will be in the interests of justice to allow such broader scope of discovery where it could aid in disposing fairly of the proceedings.
@ref O 11 r 1(4) (src:1123)
GIVEN `a broader scope of discovery could aid in disposing fairly of the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 11 r 1(4) it will be in the interests of justice to allow a broader scope of discovery` MEANS
    IF `a broader scope of discovery could aid in disposing fairly of the proceedings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where it could aid in disposing fairly of the proceedings" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b)); a lawyer could read the "where" as a sufficient condition that leaves other grounds open, which would give NOTHING here [marginal-a]

DECLARE `o 11 r 1(5) a consideration` IS ONE OF
    `o 11 r 1(5) the Ideals`
    `o 11 r 1(5) paragraph (4)`
    `o 11 r 1(5) paragraph (2)`
    `o 11 r 1(5) any other consideration`

-- src:1124 | (5) Where there is an application for a broader scope of discovery, paragraph (2) does not apply and the Court must have regard only to the Ideals and to paragraph (4).
@ref O 11 r 1(5) (src:1124)
GIVEN `there is an application for a broader scope of discovery` IS A BOOLEAN
      consideration IS A `o 11 r 1(5) a consideration`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 11 r 1(5) the Court must have regard to this on an application for a broader scope of discovery` MEANS
    IF `there is an application for a broader scope of discovery`
    THEN
        CONSIDER consideration
        WHEN `o 11 r 1(5) the Ideals` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 11 r 1(5) paragraph (4)` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 11 r 1(5) paragraph (2)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "paragraph (2) does not apply" (flat negative, ruling N2)
        WHEN `o 11 r 1(5) any other consideration` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Court must have regard only to the Ideals and to paragraph (4)"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where there is an application for a broader scope of discovery" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b)); this paragraph is not what puts the Ideals before the Court otherwise: see paragraph (2)

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 11, Rule 2 -- order for production`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:1126 | 2. —(1) The Court may, at a case conference, order that the parties in an action must within 14 days after the date of the case conference, exchange a list of and a copy of all documents in their possession or control, which fall within one or more of the following categories: ( a )
@ref O 11 r 2(1) (src:1126)
GIVEN `the order is made at a case conference` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 11 r 2(1) the Court may order the parties to exchange a list of and a copy of the documents` MEANS
    IF `the order is made at a case conference`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Court may, at a case conference, order"; for another occasion see Rules 3 and 4 [marginal-b]

-- src:1126 | 2. —(1) The Court may, at a case conference, order that the parties in an action must within 14 days after the date of the case conference, exchange a list of and a copy of all documents in their possession or control, which fall within one or more of the following categories: ( a )
@ref O 11 r 2(1) (src:1126)
`o 11 r 2(1) fourteen days after the date of the case conference` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

DECLARE `o 11 r 2(1) a category of documents` IS ONE OF
    `o 11 r 2(1)(a) all documents that the party in question will be relying on`
    `o 11 r 2(1)(b) all known adverse documents`
    `o 11 r 2(1)(c)(i) documents within a broader scope of discovery as may be agreed between the parties or any set of parties`
    `o 11 r 2(1)(c)(ii) documents within a broader scope of discovery as ordered by the Court`
    `o 11 r 2(1) any other document`

-- src:1126 | 2. —(1) The Court may, at a case conference, order that the parties in an action must within 14 days after the date of the case conference, exchange a list of and a copy of all documents in their possession or control, which fall within one or more of the following categories: ( a )
-- src:1127 | all documents that the party in question will be relying on;
-- src:1128 | ( b )
-- src:1129 | all known adverse documents;
-- src:1130 | ( c )
-- src:1131 | where applicable, documents that fall within a broader scope of discovery — (i)
-- src:1132 | as may be agreed between the parties or any set of parties; or
-- src:1133 | (ii)
-- src:1134 | as ordered by the Court.
@ref O 11 r 2(1) (src:1126-1134)
GIVEN `the document is in the party's possession or control` IS A BOOLEAN
      category IS A `o 11 r 2(1) a category of documents`
      `a broader scope of discovery applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 11 r 2(1) the document falls within a category the order may cover` MEANS
    IF NOT `the document is in the party's possession or control`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "all documents in their possession or control": a document that is not in the party's possession or control is outside the order
    ELSE
        CONSIDER category
        WHEN `o 11 r 2(1)(a) all documents that the party in question will be relying on` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 11 r 2(1)(b) all known adverse documents` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 11 r 2(1)(c)(i) documents within a broader scope of discovery as may be agreed between the parties or any set of parties` THEN
            IF `a broader scope of discovery applies`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where applicable" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
        WHEN `o 11 r 2(1)(c)(ii) documents within a broader scope of discovery as ordered by the Court` THEN
            IF `a broader scope of discovery applies`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where applicable" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
        WHEN `o 11 r 2(1) any other document` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (1) covers documents "which fall within one or more of the following categories"; Rules 3 and 4 give other powers [marginal-b]

DECLARE `o 11 r 2(1) party` IS ONE OF
    `o 11 r 2(1) each party to the action`

DECLARE `o 11 r 2(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `o 11 r 2(1) exchange a list of and a copy of the documents`

-- src:1126 | 2. —(1) The Court may, at a case conference, order that the parties in an action must within 14 days after the date of the case conference, exchange a list of and a copy of all documents in their possession or control, which fall within one or more of the following categories: ( a )
@ref O 11 r 2(1) (src:1126)
GIVEN `the Court has ordered at a case conference that the parties exchange documents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 11 r 2(1) the parties must exchange a list of and a copy of the documents` MEANS
    IF `the Court has ordered at a case conference that the parties exchange documents`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is "order[ed]" by the Court "at a case conference"; the text does not say what the parties must do without the order [marginal-b]

-- src:1126 | 2. —(1) The Court may, at a case conference, order that the parties in an action must within 14 days after the date of the case conference, exchange a list of and a copy of all documents in their possession or control, which fall within one or more of the following categories: ( a )
@ref O 11 r 2(1) (src:1126)
GIVEN `the date the parties exchange the list and the copies` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 11 r 2(1) the parties exchange the list and the copies in time` MEANS
    IF `the date the parties exchange the list and the copies` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 14 days after the date of the case conference" (a period the text fixes in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05, (a))

-- src:1126 | 2. —(1) The Court may, at a case conference, order that the parties in an action must within 14 days after the date of the case conference, exchange a list of and a copy of all documents in their possession or control, which fall within one or more of the following categories: ( a )
@ref O 11 r 2(1) (src:1126)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 11 r 2(1) party` `o 11 r 2(1) act`
`o 11 r 2(1) each party must exchange a list of and a copy of the documents` MEANS
    PARTY `o 11 r 2(1) each party to the action`
    MUST `o 11 r 2(1) exchange a list of and a copy of the documents`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 11 r 2(1) each party to the action` BECAUSE "the list and the copies were not exchanged within 14 days after the date of the case conference"

-- Paragraph (2): "includes" opens a definition, so a document that is neither answers NOTHING.
-- src:1135 | (2) In this Order, “known adverse documents” includes documents which a party ought reasonably to know are adverse to the party’s case.
@ref O 11 r 2(2) (src:1135)
GIVEN `the party knows that the document is adverse to the party's case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party ought reasonably to know that the document is adverse to the party's case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 11 r 2(2) a document is a known adverse document` MEANS
    IF `the party knows that the document is adverse to the party's case` OR `the party ought reasonably to know that the document is adverse to the party's case`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (open definition): ""known adverse documents" includes documents which a party ought reasonably to know are adverse to the party's case"; "includes" does not close the term

-- src:1136 | (3) A copy of any document may be in paper form or, if in an electronic form, in a common electronic format that the other party can use.
@ref O 11 r 2(3) (src:1136)
GIVEN `the copy is in paper form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy is in an electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in a common electronic format that the other party can use` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 11 r 2(3) the copy is in a form allowed` MEANS
    IF `the copy is in paper form`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        IF `the copy is in an electronic form` AND `it is in a common electronic format that the other party can use`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be in paper form or, if in an electronic form, in a common electronic format that the other party can use"

-- src:1137 | (4) To comply with an order made by the Court under paragraph (1), it is not necessary for the parties to exchange documents common to them that are in their possession or control to avoid duplication and to save costs.
@ref O 11 r 2(4) (src:1137)
GIVEN `the document is common to the parties and is in their possession or control` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 11 r 2(4) it is necessary to exchange the document to comply with the order` MEANS
    IF `the document is common to the parties and is in their possession or control`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is not necessary for the parties to exchange documents common to them that are in their possession or control to avoid duplication and to save costs" (flat negative, ruling N2)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph says only that a common document need not be exchanged; for any other document paragraph (1) decides [marginal-b]

-- src:1138 | (5) The parties may not rely on any document that was not exchanged or produced under this Order.
@ref O 11 r 2(5) (src:1138)
GIVEN `the document was exchanged or produced under this Order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 11 r 2(5) the party may rely on the document` MEANS
    IF NOT `the document was exchanged or produced under this Order`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The parties may not rely on any document that was not exchanged or produced under this Order" (flat negative, ruling N2)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is for a document "not exchanged or produced under this Order"; for one that was, Rules 8 and 10 and the rest of the Rules decide [marginal-b]

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 11, Rule 3 -- production of requested documents`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:1140 | 3. —(1) The Court may order any party to produce the original or a copy of a specific document or class of documents (called the requested documents) in the party’s possession or control, if the requesting party — ( a )
-- src:1141 | properly identifies the requested documents; and
-- src:1142 | ( b )
-- src:1143 | shows that the requested documents are material to the issues in the case.
@ref O 11 r 3(1) (src:1140-1143)
GIVEN `the requested documents are in the party's possession or control` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requesting party properly identifies the requested documents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requesting party shows that the requested documents are material to the issues in the case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 11 r 3(1) the Court may order any party to produce the requested documents` MEANS
    IF `the requested documents are in the party's possession or control` AND `the requesting party properly identifies the requested documents` AND `the requesting party shows that the requested documents are material to the issues in the case`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the original or a copy of a specific document or class of documents ... in the party's possession or control, if the requesting party properly identifies the requested documents; and shows that the requested documents are material to the issues in the case" (an "if" that fails, reading (a) of the rule of 2026-10-29) [marginal-a]

-- "(called the requested documents)": the term is defined here for the rest of the Order.
-- src:1140 | 3. —(1) The Court may order any party to produce the original or a copy of a specific document or class of documents (called the requested documents) in the party’s possession or control, if the requesting party — ( a )
@ref O 11 r 3(1) (src:1140)
GIVEN `it is a specific document or class of documents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court orders a party to produce the original or a copy of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 11 r 3(1) a document or class of documents is the requested documents` MEANS
    IF `it is a specific document or class of documents` AND `the Court orders a party to produce the original or a copy of it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a specific document or class of documents (called the requested documents)" (a definition that says "called")

DECLARE `o 11 r 3(2) a matter the affidavit may be ordered to state` IS ONE OF
    `o 11 r 3(2) that the requested documents are not in the party's possession or control`
    `o 11 r 3(2) whether that party had such possession or control previously`
    `o 11 r 3(2) when that party parted with possession or control`
    `o 11 r 3(2) what has become of the requested documents`

-- src:1144 | (2) If the requested documents are not in the party’s possession or control, the Court may order that party to file an affidavit stating this, as well as whether that party had such possession or control previously and if so, when that party parted with possession or control and what has become of the requested documents.
@ref O 11 r 3(2) (src:1144)
GIVEN `the requested documents are not in the party's possession or control` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `o 11 r 3(2) a matter the affidavit may be ordered to state`
      `that party had such possession or control previously` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 11 r 3(2) the Court may order the party to file an affidavit stating this` MEANS
    IF `the requested documents are not in the party's possession or control`
    THEN
        CONSIDER matter
        WHEN `o 11 r 3(2) that the requested documents are not in the party's possession or control` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 11 r 3(2) whether that party had such possession or control previously` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 11 r 3(2) when that party parted with possession or control` THEN
            IF `that party had such possession or control previously`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and if so, when that party parted with possession or control" (an "if" that fails: the party never had possession, so there is nothing to say about when it parted with it; ruling of 2026-11-05, "if" like "where") [marginal-a]
        WHEN `o 11 r 3(2) what has become of the requested documents` THEN
            IF `that party had such possession or control previously`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and if so, ... what has become of the requested documents" (an "if" that fails, as for the date it parted with them) [marginal-a]
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the requested documents are not in the party's possession or control" fails [marginal-a]

-- src:1145 | (3) Except in a special case, if the Court orders the parties to file and serve affidavits of evidence in chief of witnesses after pleadings have been filed and served but before any exchange of documents, the Court must not exercise its power under this Rule before the parties comply with the Court’s order.
@ref O 11 r 3(3) (src:1145)
GIVEN `it is a special case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court orders the parties to file and serve affidavits of evidence in chief of witnesses after pleadings have been filed and served but before any exchange of documents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parties have complied with the Court's order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 11 r 3 the Court may exercise its power under this Rule` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it is a special case`) AND `the Court orders the parties to file and serve affidavits of evidence in chief of witnesses after pleadings have been filed and served but before any exchange of documents` AND (NOT `the parties have complied with the Court's order`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except in a special case, if the Court orders the parties to file and serve affidavits of evidence in chief ... the Court must not exercise its power under this Rule before the parties comply with the Court's order" (flat negative, ruling N2)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is for a case that is not a special case, after such an order and before compliance; outside it paragraph (3) is silent [marginal-b]

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 11, Rules 4 and 5 -- the Court's power to order production; no order for production of certain documents`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:1149 | 5. —(1) Except in a special case, the Court must not order production of any document that merely leads a party on a train of inquiry to other documents. (2) The Court must not order the production of any document that is part of a party’s private or internal correspondence, whether in paper form or in an electronic format (including electronic mail, short message service or any instant messaging service), wherever such correspondence may be stored unless — ( a )
@ref O 11 r 5(1) (src:1149)
GIVEN `it is a special case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document merely leads a party on a train of inquiry to other documents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 11 r 5(1) the Court may order production of the document` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it is a special case`) AND `the document merely leads a party on a train of inquiry to other documents`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except in a special case, the Court must not order production of any document that merely leads a party on a train of inquiry to other documents" (flat negative, ruling N2)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is for a document that "merely leads a party on a train of inquiry" outside a special case; outside it paragraph (1) is silent [marginal-b]

-- src:1149 | 5. —(1) Except in a special case, the Court must not order production of any document that merely leads a party on a train of inquiry to other documents. (2) The Court must not order the production of any document that is part of a party’s private or internal correspondence, whether in paper form or in an electronic format (including electronic mail, short message service or any instant messaging service), wherever such correspondence may be stored unless — ( a )
-- src:1150 | it is a special case; or
-- src:1151 | ( b )
-- src:1152 | such correspondence are known adverse documents.
@ref O 11 r 5(2) (src:1149-1152)
GIVEN `the document is part of a party's private or internal correspondence, whether in paper form or in an electronic format` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a special case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the correspondence is a known adverse document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 11 r 5(2) the Court may order the production of the document` MEANS
    IF `the document is part of a party's private or internal correspondence, whether in paper form or in an electronic format` AND (NOT `it is a special case`) AND (NOT `the correspondence is a known adverse document`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Court must not order the production of any document that is part of a party's private or internal correspondence ... unless (a) it is a special case; or (b) such correspondence are known adverse documents" (flat negative, ruling N2)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is for private or internal correspondence "unless" (a) or (b); outside it paragraph (2) is silent [marginal-b]

-- src:1153 | (3) Subject to any written law, the Court must not order the production of any document which is subject to any privilege or where its production would be contrary to the public interest.
@ref O 11 r 5(3) (src:1153)
GIVEN `a written law provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is subject to any privilege` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its production would be contrary to the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 11 r 5(3) the Court may order the production of the document` MEANS
    IF (NOT `a written law provides otherwise`) AND (`the document is subject to any privilege` OR `its production would be contrary to the public interest`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to any written law, the Court must not order the production of any document which is subject to any privilege or where its production would be contrary to the public interest" (flat negative, ruling N2)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is "subject to any written law" and for a document that is privileged or whose production would be contrary to the public interest; outside it paragraph (3) is silent [marginal-b]

-- Rule 5 gathered: any of its three prohibitions that says no is the answer; otherwise Rule 5 does not answer.
-- src:1149 | 5. —(1) Except in a special case, the Court must not order production of any document that merely leads a party on a train of inquiry to other documents. (2) The Court must not order the production of any document that is part of a party’s private or internal correspondence, whether in paper form or in an electronic format (including electronic mail, short message service or any instant messaging service), wherever such correspondence may be stored unless — ( a )
-- src:1150 | it is a special case; or
-- src:1151 | ( b )
-- src:1152 | such correspondence are known adverse documents.
-- src:1153 | (3) Subject to any written law, the Court must not order the production of any document which is subject to any privilege or where its production would be contrary to the public interest.
@ref O 11 r 5 (src:1149-1153)
GIVEN `paragraph (1) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (2) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (3) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 11 r 5 the Court may order the production of the document` MEANS
    IF `paragraph (1) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `paragraph (2) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `paragraph (3) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): one of paragraphs (1), (2) and (3) says the Court must not order production
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): none of the prohibitions in Rule 5 reaches the document, and Rule 5 gives no power of its own [marginal-b]

-- src:1147 | 4. Subject to Rules 5, 8 and 9, the Court may, of its own accord and at any time, order any party or non‑party to produce a copy of any document that is in the person’s possession or control.
@ref O 11 r 4 (src:1147)
GIVEN `the document is in the person's possession or control` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Rule 5 answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `Rule 8 answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `Rule 9 answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 11 r 4 the Court may order any party or non-party to produce a copy of the document` MEANS
    IF `Rule 5 answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `Rule 8 answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `Rule 9 answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to Rules 5, 8 and 9": one of them says no
    ELSE
        IF `the document is in the person's possession or control`
        THEN JUST TRUE -- the power is "of its own accord and at any time": no input for the occasion, because none limits it
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any document that is in the person's possession or control" [marginal-b]

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 11, Rules 6 and 7 -- continuing duty to produce; non-compliance with production order`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:1155 | 6. Where the Court makes an order under Rule 2, 3 or 4, the party required to produce the documents remains under a duty to produce any of those documents within 14 days after that document comes into the party’s possession or control at any time in the course of the proceedings.
@ref O 11 r 6 (src:1155)
GIVEN `the Court makes an order under Rule 2, 3 or 4` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 11 r 6 the party required to produce the documents remains under a duty to produce further documents` MEANS
    IF `the Court makes an order under Rule 2, 3 or 4`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the Court makes an order under Rule 2, 3 or 4" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))

-- src:1155 | 6. Where the Court makes an order under Rule 2, 3 or 4, the party required to produce the documents remains under a duty to produce any of those documents within 14 days after that document comes into the party’s possession or control at any time in the course of the proceedings.
@ref O 11 r 6 (src:1155)
`o 11 r 6 fourteen days after the document comes into the party's possession or control` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- src:1155 | 6. Where the Court makes an order under Rule 2, 3 or 4, the party required to produce the documents remains under a duty to produce any of those documents within 14 days after that document comes into the party’s possession or control at any time in the course of the proceedings.
@ref O 11 r 6 (src:1155)
GIVEN `the date the party produces the document` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 11 r 6 the party produces the document in time` MEANS
    IF `the date the party produces the document` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 14 days after that document comes into the party's possession or control" (a period the text fixes in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05, (a))

DECLARE `o 11 r 6 party` IS ONE OF
    `o 11 r 6 the party required to produce the documents`

DECLARE `o 11 r 6 act` IS ONE OF
    `o 11 r 6 produce the document`

-- src:1155 | 6. Where the Court makes an order under Rule 2, 3 or 4, the party required to produce the documents remains under a duty to produce any of those documents within 14 days after that document comes into the party’s possession or control at any time in the course of the proceedings.
@ref O 11 r 6 (src:1155)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 11 r 6 party` `o 11 r 6 act`
`o 11 r 6 the party required to produce must produce a document that comes into the party's possession or control` MEANS
    PARTY `o 11 r 6 the party required to produce the documents`
    MUST `o 11 r 6 produce the document`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 11 r 6 the party required to produce the documents` BECAUSE "the document was not produced within 14 days after it came into the party's possession or control"

DECLARE `o 11 r 7 a thing the Court may do` IS ONE OF
    `o 11 r 7(a) order that the action be dismissed or that the defence be struck out and judgment be entered accordingly`
    `o 11 r 7(b) draw an adverse inference or make any such order as the Court deems fit`
    `o 11 r 7(c) punish that party for contempt of court`
    `o 11 r 7(d) order that that party may not rely on any document that is within the scope of the order unless the Court approves`

-- src:1157 | 7. If any party fails to comply with any order made by the Court under this Order, the Court may — ( a )
-- src:1158 | order that the action be dismissed or that the defence be struck out and judgment be entered accordingly;
-- src:1159 | ( b )
-- src:1160 | draw an adverse inference or make any such order as the Court deems fit;
-- src:1161 | ( c )
-- src:1162 | punish that party for contempt of court if the order has been served on that party’s solicitor, but it is open to that party to show that that party was not notified or did not know about the order; or
-- src:1163 | ( d )
-- src:1164 | order that that party may not rely on any document that is within the scope of the order unless the Court approves.
@ref O 11 r 7 (src:1157-1164)
GIVEN `a party fails to comply with an order made by the Court under this Order` IS A BOOLEAN
      thing IS A `o 11 r 7 a thing the Court may do`
      `the order has been served on that party's solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that party shows that that party was not notified or did not know about the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 11 r 7 the Court may do this` MEANS
    IF `a party fails to comply with an order made by the Court under this Order`
    THEN
        CONSIDER thing
        WHEN `o 11 r 7(a) order that the action be dismissed or that the defence be struck out and judgment be entered accordingly` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 11 r 7(b) draw an adverse inference or make any such order as the Court deems fit` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 11 r 7(c) punish that party for contempt of court` THEN
            IF `the order has been served on that party's solicitor`
            THEN
                IF `that party shows that that party was not notified or did not know about the order`
                THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is open to that party to show that that party was not notified or did not know about the order" [marginal-a]
                ELSE JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the order has been served on that party's solicitor" (an "if" that fails) [marginal-a]
        WHEN `o 11 r 7(d) order that that party may not rely on any document that is within the scope of the order unless the Court approves` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If any party fails to comply with any order made by the Court under this Order" fails [marginal-a]

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 11, Rules 8 to 10 -- privileged and confidential documents; use of documents in other proceedings`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:1166 | 8. —(1) A document which was at any time subject to any privilege must not be relied on unless the party entitled to the privilege consents or the Court approves. (2) Such a document does not lose its privilege or confidentiality even if it was disclosed or taken inadvertently or unlawfully by anyone.
@ref O 11 r 8(1) (src:1166)
GIVEN `the document was at any time subject to any privilege` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party entitled to the privilege consents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court approves` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 11 r 8(1) the document may be relied on` MEANS
    IF `the document was at any time subject to any privilege` AND (NOT `the party entitled to the privilege consents`) AND (NOT `the Court approves`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A document which was at any time subject to any privilege must not be relied on unless the party entitled to the privilege consents or the Court approves" (flat negative, ruling N2)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is for a privileged document "unless" consent or approval; outside it paragraph (1) is silent [marginal-b]

-- src:1166 | 8. —(1) A document which was at any time subject to any privilege must not be relied on unless the party entitled to the privilege consents or the Court approves. (2) Such a document does not lose its privilege or confidentiality even if it was disclosed or taken inadvertently or unlawfully by anyone.
@ref O 11 r 8(2) (src:1166)
GIVEN `the document is one within paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was disclosed or taken inadvertently or unlawfully by anyone` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 11 r 8(2) the document loses its privilege or confidentiality` MEANS
    IF `the document is one within paragraph (1)` AND `it was disclosed or taken inadvertently or unlawfully by anyone`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Such a document does not lose its privilege or confidentiality even if it was disclosed or taken inadvertently or unlawfully by anyone" (flat negative, ruling N2)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Such a document" and "even if it was disclosed or taken inadvertently or unlawfully"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

-- src:1168 | 9. —(1) A party who is required by any order made by the Court under this Order to produce documents may not withhold or object to the production of any document on the ground that the document is confidential. (2) A confidential document does not lose its confidentiality even if it was disclosed or taken inadvertently or unlawfully by anyone.
@ref O 11 r 9(1) (src:1168)
GIVEN `the party is required by an order made by the Court under this Order to produce documents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ground is that the document is confidential` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 11 r 9(1) the party may withhold or object to the production of the document on this ground` MEANS
    IF `the party is required by an order made by the Court under this Order to produce documents` AND `the ground is that the document is confidential`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A party who is required by any order made by the Court under this Order to produce documents may not withhold or object to the production of any document on the ground that the document is confidential" (flat negative, ruling N2)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is for a party required by an order under this Order, and for the ground of confidentiality; other grounds (for example privilege, Rule 8) are for other provisions [marginal-b]

-- src:1168 | 9. —(1) A party who is required by any order made by the Court under this Order to produce documents may not withhold or object to the production of any document on the ground that the document is confidential. (2) A confidential document does not lose its confidentiality even if it was disclosed or taken inadvertently or unlawfully by anyone.
@ref O 11 r 9(2) (src:1168)
GIVEN `the document is a confidential document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was disclosed or taken inadvertently or unlawfully by anyone` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 11 r 9(2) the document loses its confidentiality` MEANS
    IF `the document is a confidential document` AND `it was disclosed or taken inadvertently or unlawfully by anyone`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A confidential document does not lose its confidentiality even if it was disclosed or taken inadvertently or unlawfully by anyone" (flat negative, ruling N2)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A confidential document" and "even if it was disclosed or taken inadvertently or unlawfully"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

-- src:1170 | 10. —(1) Any document produced under this Order or by compulsion of law in the court proceedings must not be relied on in other proceedings by the other parties or non‑parties unless the party who produced the document consents or the Court otherwise approves. (2) The party who used or produced any document in a case may apply to the Court to prohibit the use of such documents for any purpose other than for that case.
@ref O 11 r 10(1) (src:1170)
GIVEN `the document was produced under this Order or by compulsion of law in the court proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is to be relied on in other proceedings by other parties or non-parties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party who produced the document consents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court otherwise approves` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 11 r 10(1) the document may be relied on in other proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the document was produced under this Order or by compulsion of law in the court proceedings` AND `it is to be relied on in other proceedings by other parties or non-parties` AND (NOT `the party who produced the document consents`) AND (NOT `the Court otherwise approves`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any document produced under this Order or by compulsion of law in the court proceedings must not be relied on in other proceedings by the other parties or non-parties unless the party who produced the document consents or the Court otherwise approves" (flat negative, ruling N2)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is for such a document, in other proceedings, "unless" consent or approval; outside it paragraph (1) is silent [marginal-b]

-- src:1170 | 10. —(1) Any document produced under this Order or by compulsion of law in the court proceedings must not be relied on in other proceedings by the other parties or non‑parties unless the party who produced the document consents or the Court otherwise approves. (2) The party who used or produced any document in a case may apply to the Court to prohibit the use of such documents for any purpose other than for that case.
@ref O 11 r 10(2) (src:1170)
GIVEN `the party used or produced the document in the case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 11 r 10(2) the party may apply to the Court to prohibit the use of the documents for any other purpose` MEANS
    IF `the party used or produced the document in the case`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The party who used or produced any document in a case"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 11, Rule 11 -- production before action or against non-parties`
-- ===========================================================================

DECLARE `o 11 r 11(1) a purpose of the order` IS ONE OF
    `o 11 r 11(1) to identify possible parties to any proceedings`
    `o 11 r 11(1) to enable a party to trace the party's property`
    `o 11 r 11(1) any other purpose`

-- src:1172 | 11. —(1) The Court may order the production of documents and information before the commencement of proceedings or against a non‑party to identify possible parties to any proceedings, to enable a party to trace the party’s property or for any other lawful purpose, in the interests of justice. (2) The Court must not order a document to be produced if its production cannot be compelled in law.
@ref O 11 r 11(1) (src:1172)
GIVEN `the order is before the commencement of proceedings or against a non-party` IS A BOOLEAN
      purpose IS A `o 11 r 11(1) a purpose of the order`
      `the other purpose is lawful` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in the interests of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 11 r 11(1) the Court may order the production of documents and information` MEANS
    IF `the order is before the commencement of proceedings or against a non-party`
    THEN
        IF `it is in the interests of justice`
        THEN
            CONSIDER purpose
            WHEN `o 11 r 11(1) to identify possible parties to any proceedings` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `o 11 r 11(1) to enable a party to trace the party's property` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `o 11 r 11(1) any other purpose` THEN
                IF `the other purpose is lawful`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for any other lawful purpose" [marginal-b]
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the interests of justice" fails [marginal-a]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "before the commencement of proceedings or against a non-party"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

-- src:1172 | 11. —(1) The Court may order the production of documents and information before the commencement of proceedings or against a non‑party to identify possible parties to any proceedings, to enable a party to trace the party’s property or for any other lawful purpose, in the interests of justice. (2) The Court must not order a document to be produced if its production cannot be compelled in law.
@ref O 11 r 11(2) (src:1172)
GIVEN `the production of the document cannot be compelled in law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 11 r 11(2) the Court may order the document to be produced` MEANS
    IF `the production of the document cannot be compelled in law`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Court must not order a document to be produced if its production cannot be compelled in law" (flat negative, ruling N2)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is for a document whose production "cannot be compelled in law"; outside it paragraph (2) is silent [marginal-b]

-- src:1173 | (3) A non‑party is entitled to all reasonable costs arising out of such an application.
@ref O 11 r 11(3) (src:1173)
GIVEN `the person is a non-party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the costs arise out of an application under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the costs are reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 11 r 11(3) the non-party is entitled to the costs` MEANS
    IF `the person is a non-party` AND `the costs arise out of an application under this Rule` AND `the costs are reasonable`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A non-party is entitled to all reasonable costs arising out of such an application"; the text does not say that no other cost is recoverable [marginal-b]

