    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- src:1175 | 12. —(1) If a party requests to inspect the original of any document produced, the party who produced the document must arrange a mutually convenient time and place for the inspection to take place. (2) Such inspection must take place within 14 days after the request unless the parties otherwise agree.
@ref O 11 r 12(2) (src:1175)
GIVEN `the parties otherwise agree` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the inspection takes place` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 11 r 12(2) the inspection takes place in time` MEANS
    IF `the parties otherwise agree`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the parties otherwise agree"; what the parties agree is for them, and the paragraph is silent [marginal-b]
    ELSE
        IF `the date the inspection takes place` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 14 days after the request" (a period the text fixes in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05, (a))

-- src:1176 | (3) If the party who produced the document fails to comply with paragraph (1) or (2), the requesting party may apply to the Court to compel that party to do so.
